== Chapter II

#align(center)[CHAP. II. Containing the grand Proposition.]

2\. I Pass to the second, the #emph[excellency] of the Priviledge: #emph[All things work together for good.] This is a #emph[Jacobs] staff in the hand of faith, with which we may walk cheerfully to the Mount of God: what will satisfy or give content, if this will not? #emph[All things work together for good.] This word συνεργεῖ #emph[work together,] is a Physical expression. Several poysonful ingredients put together, being tempered by the skill of the Apothecary, make a Soveraign Medicine, and work together for the good of the Patient#footnote[#emph[Venena ex corporibus per venenata pharmaca educunt medici.] Pet. Mart.]. So all Gods Providences being divinely tempered and sanctified, do work together for the best to the Saints. He who #emph[loves God,] and is #emph[called according to his purpose,] may say to his soul, #emph[Soul take thy ease,] for, #emph[there is much good laid up for thee,] every thing in the world shall be for thy good. This is a Christians #emph[Cordial,] which may cause the colour to come in his face, and make him like #emph[Jonathan,] who when he had tasted the #emph[honey] at the end of the rod #emph[his eyes were enlightened,] 1 Sam 14 27. Why should a Christian exenterate himself? Why should he kill himself with care, when all things shall sweetly concur, yea conspire for his good? The result of the Text is this,

#emph[Doct.] That all the various dealings of God with his Children,#footnote[Doct.] do by a special Providence turn to their good#footnote[Nemo qui sit Christianus de rerum catastrophe debet ambigere. #emph[P. Mart.]].

Ps 25:10. #emph[All the paths of the Lord are mercy unto such as keep his Covenant.] If every path hath mercy in it, then it works for good.

